# Agent workflow (principal engineer)

Use this on every non-trivial task. This is the **single spine** for how agents work.  
Rule map: `docs/internal/cursor-rules-read-order.md`. Full playbook: `docs/internal/principal-engineer-playbook.md`.

## Context order (do not skip)

1. `graft ask "<task>" --source` — top hit is the edit target unless the task is exhaustive search (`graft grep`).
2. Follow **this** rule’s checklist. Then open only the **scoped** rules that match the work (API → `api-route-authz.mdc`; UI → `global-style-guide.mdc` — **CAALM palette first**, even when the spec includes or omits CSS; security → `security-rbac.mdc`; schema → `caalm-demo-database-sync.mdc`; Appwrite IDs → `appwrite-collection-ids.mdc`; product copy → `writing.mdc`).
3. `@`-reference canonical files; do not paste large blobs into chat.
4. MCP: prefer **Appwrite** for DB schema/data, **GitHub** for PR/CI. For live CAALM page checks in Cursor, use the **in-IDE Browser Tab** (`cursor-ide-browser`): `browser_navigate` with `position: "active"` so the pane is visible. Cookies persist per workspace after one sign-in in that tab. Do **not** attach Cursor Playwright MCP to Claude's Chrome on port 9222. Claude Code keeps that Chrome (`scripts/start-chrome-debug.ps1`). Use `pnpm test:e2e` for automated Playwright tests, not for in-IDE inspection.

## Do not add rule sprawl

- Prefer **file-scoped** rules (`globs`) over new `alwaysApply: true` rules.
- Do not create a second “workflow / how to agent” always-on rule that duplicates this file.
- UI details (dialogs, buttons, inputs, segmented switches, Tailwind colors) live only in `global-style-guide.mdc` — do not revive split UI rule files.
- Chat tone: `plain-english-junior-dev.mdc`. Product/docs marketing copy: `writing.mdc` (scoped).

## Delivery checklist (features touching data or auth)

- [ ] Tenant/org scope on every query and mutation (no cross-tenant reads).
- [ ] Permission gate: `pnpm new:api-route …` or existing `requirePermission` pattern — **no role bypasses**.
- [ ] Audit narrative for material writes (who, what, when, tenant) — `audit-narrative.mdc` / `logAuditEvent`.
- [ ] Schema change → prod first, then `node scripts/sync-demo-database-schema.mjs --apply`, zero diff on dry run.
- [ ] `.env.example` placeholders only; never commit live IDs/secrets.

## Review loop before “done”

1. `pnpm run test:api-authz` when API routes or permissions change.
2. Targeted `pnpm test:unit` for touched modules.
3. Playwright smoke on changed user journeys when UI/routing changes (`pnpm test:e2e` or Playwright MCP locally).
4. Fix CI failures with `fix-ci` / team-kit mindset — do not disable gates.

## Scope discipline

- Smallest correct diff; no drive-by refactors.
- Modular monolith: keep domain logic in `src/lib/<domain>/`; routes stay thin.
- Desktop-first: no full phone layouts for dense admin unless companion route.

## Cloud agents

- Project `.cursor/hooks.json` only (user hooks may not run).
- Use Team MCP for Appwrite/GitHub/Vercel when cloud lacks local MCP.
- Open PR on `cursor/<name>-0e5f`; push before heavy testing.

## Prompt templates

On Plan mode or “make a plan”: follow `.cursor/rules/plan-prompt-templates.mdc` (auto-pick A–J when clear; else ask A–K with K = Other). Fill brackets **in memory only** — never rewrite `.cursor/prompt-templates/*.md`.
